## Setup

Install [Homebrew](https://brew.sh), then run in the repository:

```sh
brew bundle
export PATH="$HOME/.ghcup/bin:$PATH"   # add this line to ~/.zshrc too
ghcup install ghc {{ghc_version}}
ghcup install cabal latest
ghcup install hls latest
cabal update
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
gh extension install github/gh-stack   # optional: stacked PRs
```

Homebrew installs ghcup, Ormolu, HLint and the GitHub CLI. ghcup installs GHC, cabal and HLS into
`~/.ghcup/bin`. Homebrew does not put that folder on `PATH`. The `export` line puts it first, so
ghcup's GHC and cabal win over any copy from Homebrew. The git hook runs the checks before each
push. `gh stack` is optional: it helps to open and update stacked PRs.

`with-compiler` in `cabal.project` names the GHC version, so cabal and HLS use it even when other
versions are installed. CI reads the same line and pins the other tools in
`.github/workflows/ci.yml`.

## Commands

```sh
scripts/check        # every quality gate: format, lint, build, test
cabal build all
cabal test all
cabal repl lib:{{package}}
ormolu --mode inplace $(find app src test -name '*.hs')
cabal install --enable-optimization   # release build: cabal.project builds with -O0
```

`scripts/check` is the single list of gates. The git hook and CI run it too.

